---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/16-10/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/16-10/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/16-10/', brochure='https://www.emerson.com/is/content/emerson/en/corporate/branson/documents/brochure-cpx-h-ultrasonic-baths-pdf.pdf';
const display=x=>Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+String(v)).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="Bransonic CPX1800H dry inspection" subtitle="" description="An interactive metric dry inspection model for an inert basket coupon." wide={true}>
<article id="dry" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/16-10/">← Equipment 16-10</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#dry-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">16-10 / Bransonic CPX1800H / Dry basket inspection</p><h2>Bransonic CPX1800H</h2><p>Check how a rigid inert part fits in a virtual lift-out basket. The ready 100 × 70 × 25 mm coupon has 14 mm clearance on each side across the width. This is dry geometry, not a cleaning simulation.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the enclosure</h3><div id="dry-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Basket','Rear'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="dry-xr" type="button" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div>
<canvas id="dry-model" aria-label="Orbitable metric tank enclosure with removable lid and lift-out basket"></canvas><p id="dry-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Click the lid to remove or replace it and the metal basket to lift or lower it. A fitting coupon appears in the raised basket. Drag, scroll or pinch to inspect. The front control panel is decorative.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Check the dry fit</h3><div class="e-row"><button id="dry-lid" type="button">Remove dry lid</button><button id="dry-basket" type="button">Lift dry basket</button><button id="dry-example" class="e-run" type="button">Open, lift and check example</button></div>
<form id="dry-form" novalidate><div class="e-fields"><label>Coupon ID<input name="sampleId" value="inert-coupon-01" maxlength="96"/></label>{[['width','Width X (mm)',100],['depth','Depth Z (mm)',70],['height','Height Y (mm)',25]].map(([k,t,x])=><label>{t}<input name={k} type="number" min=".1" max="180" step="any" value={x}/></label>)}</div>
<div class="e-row"><button id="dry-fit" class="e-run" type="submit">Check dry fit</button><button id="dry-rotate" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Toggle quarter turn</button><button id="dry-oversize" type="button">Set wider coupon</button><button id="dry-reset" type="button">Reset station</button></div></form><p id="dry-status" role="status">Lid in place. Basket seated.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Read the clearances</h3><p id="dry-result" role="status">No dry fit evaluated.</p><div class="e-row"><button id="dry-fit-json" disabled>Fit JSON</button><button id="dry-audit" disabled>Replay interrupted mock log</button><button id="dry-audit-json" disabled>Mock log JSON</button></div><p id="dry-audit-result" role="status">No mock audit replayed.</p>
<p>“Replay” demonstrates a prerecorded administrative state transition only: the record stops at 20 virtual seconds of a synthetic 60-second entry, marked interrupted, with no completed entry. Nothing runs or gets cleaned. <a href={a+'example-fit.json'}>Example fit</a> · <a href={a+'example-audit.json'}>Example mock log</a>.</p></section>
<section><h3>Model geometry and scope</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original compact CPX1800H envelope"/><figcaption>Original reconstruction of the CPX1800H outer silhouette and raised control tower.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original tank, parked lid and raised dry basket"/><figcaption>Original lid, basket and coupon illustration. Basket dimensions and parked positions are design values.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Housing size</td><td>251 × 304 × 302 mm (width × depth × height)</td><td><a href={brochure}>Emerson, CPX-H brochure, specifications p. 2</a>; small details such as ports are inferred.</td></tr><tr><td>Tank opening and depth</td><td>150 × 140 × 100 mm</td><td><a href={brochure}>Brochure, Model 1800 column</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>Clear basket volume</td><td>128 × 112 × 74 mm</td><td>Original simplified mesh basket, not an approved or measured accessory.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>This centered rigid-box model compares X, Z and Y extents. A quarter turn swaps X and Z; each horizontal side allowance is half the difference, while headroom is one-sided above the floor. Zero is counted as a nominal fit. This does not check an insertion trajectory, corner form, deformability or real material compatibility. It contains no bath chemistry, sonics, heat, controls, hardware or cleanliness prediction.</p></section>
<section id="dry-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{display(x.expected)}</td><td>{display(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'bransonic-1800.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Interaction targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles, {m.draws} draw primitives; optional WebXR, physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/16-10/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#dry header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#dry h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#dry section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#dry button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#dry button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#dry-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#dry-chart{width:100%;max-height:16rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#dry table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#dry td,#dry th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#dry figure{margin:0}#dry img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
#dry caption{text-align:left}#dry input,#dry select,#dry button{min-width:0}#dry .e-hint{font-size:.92rem}</style>
